# What must not go into the image, in the order of how much it would matter.

# Your network. storage/ holds the four SQLite files, and the primary one is a
# description of your own LAN — every address, every hostname, every service
# you have drawn. It belongs in a volume on your machine and nowhere else,
# least of all in a layer that could be pushed somewhere.
/storage

# The key to config/credentials.yml.enc. Nothing in the image reads the
# credentials — bin/docker-entrypoint generates a secret_key_base instead — so
# the key has no reason to be here, and a secret with no reason to be somewhere
# is a secret to leave out.
/config/master.key
/.env*

# Rebuilt during the build, and a stale copy would win the COPY.
/public/assets
/tmp
/log
/.bundle
/vendor/bundle

# Nothing the running app reads. The test group is not installed in the image,
# so the suite could not run in here even if it were copied.
/.git
/.github
/test
/doc
/.gitattributes
/.gitignore
/.rubocop.yml

# Editor and OS leavings.
.DS_Store
*.swp
